in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @io

# @io/crypto — the cryptographic-primitive @io species (mirror-
# altitude lift-tick of the boot-floor grammar).
#
# Sibling to @io/cargo (2026-06-05; the first mirror-altitude @io
# species), @io/stagefreight (2026-06-23), @io/oci (2026-06-24),
# @io/git (2026-06-24), @io/algebra (2026-06-30). Same species
# shape at the crypto-primitive altitude: typed contract the mirror
# side sees; opaque non-mirror body (vendor crypto: sha2, sha1,
# ed25519-dalek, age, ssh-key) discharging at the realisation
# boundary.
#
# === Landing metadata ===
#
# Landed 2026-07-15 by Mara as Landing 6 of the @secrets shape-
# proposal sequence (companion audit: `docs/audits/2026-07-15-seam-
# secrets-shape-proposal-phase-d-cascade.md` at 019ad8f, ratifying
# Candidate 2 as Mara-mintable per @io/{cargo, git, oci,
# stagefreight, algebra} five-instance precedent chain). Companion
# shape-proposal at `docs/scouts/2026-07-15-mara-secrets-shape-
# proposal.md` §5.5 revised step 6 (Seam §D9 REED-INLINE
# addition).
#
# === The lift-tick recognition ===
#
# @io/crypto has been declared at BOOT-FLOOR grammar altitude only:
# `boot/std/io/crypto.mirror` (2026-06-01) carries `grammar
# @io/crypto` with sha1 / sha256 / ed25519_sign / ed25519_verify
# primitives. `shards/io.mirror` 161-162 verbatim names the
# discipline at family-root altitude:
#
#   "@io/crypto     hash + signature + AEAD over bytes. Vendor
#                    surface (sha2, age, ssh-key)."
#
# But no `shards/io/crypto.mirror` mirror-altitude species-decl
# existed. Seam's Phase D-cascade §D9 surfaced the cite drift:
# @io/secrets/sops requires @io/crypto at mirror-altitude for its
# age-backend composition (per `docs/scouts/2026-07-15-mara-
# secrets-shape-proposal.md` §2.7); boot-floor grammar cannot
# compose-from-mirror-altitude as a species (grammar-vs-species
# altitude type-shape mismatch).
#
# This shard is the substrate-honest lift-tick: pull @io/crypto
# from boot-floor grammar to mirror-altitude species-decl,
# preserving the boot-floor's four primitives, extending to the
# AEAD + age + ssh-key vendor surface io.mirror 161-162 named. The
# boot shard is RETAINED, not retired (same pattern as
# @mirror/data/json + boot/std/data/json.mirror; consumer-pull
# migration is a separate tick).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# The word `@io/crypto` is substrate-decl'd across four altitudes
# with landed carriers:
#
#   1. `boot/std/io/crypto.mirror` (2026-06-01) — boot-floor
#      `grammar @io/crypto` with sha1, sha256, ed25519_sign,
#      ed25519_verify primitives; the operational floor since the
#      bootstrap era.
#
#   2. `shards/io.mirror` 161-162 verbatim — family-root
#      substrate-decl naming the discipline ("hash + signature +
#      AEAD over bytes. Vendor surface (sha2, age, ssh-key).").
#
#   3. `docs/insights/2026-05-26-glass-wall-and-cross-wall-
#      kintsugi.md` §"What stays in @io permanently" — SHA-1 named
#      as permanent @io resident for git interop; SHA-256 lives at
#      the boundary because canonical impl is vendor crypto
#      (sha2 crate intrinsics); ed25519 is permanent @io (field
#      arithmetic is opaque vendor code by necessity).
#
#   4. Alex 2026-07-14 SSH-signing design intent (verbatim from
#      `shards/subject/visibility/sheaf.mirror` 21-32): "Each peer
#      has their own key ... Only connected through Fractal.Lens."
#      Peer keys ARE ssh-key vendor surface; @io/crypto lifts the
#      typed contract for that surface at mirror altitude.
#
# The ~61st instance of [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-
# word]] on landing — the primitive has been operational since
# 2026-06-01; this shard names the mirror-altitude species that
# consumers already assumed existed.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (substrate-decl):
#   @io                       — family-root; the boundary-with-non-
#                               mirror discipline; five-op prism +
#                               opacity + imperfect return shape.
#
# Consumers (compose over this species):
#   @io/secrets               — key-gated projection; consumes
#                               ssh_key / age_key material via
#                               key_material_ref carriers.
#   @io/secrets/sops          — SOPS vendor sub-species; consumes
#                               age + pgp + kms recipients via
#                               aead_encrypt / aead_decrypt +
#                               signature primitives.
#   @io/git                   — git object hashing (per @io/git
#                               hash_well_formed sub-bilateral);
#                               composes sha1 (SHA1-mode repos) +
#                               sha256 (SHA256-mode repos).
#   @fragmentation            — content-addressing via sha256 (per
#                               boot floor docstring: future
#                               re-route deferred).
#
# === Cross-wall-kintsugi candidacy partition ===
#
# Per `docs/insights/2026-05-26-glass-wall-and-cross-wall-
# kintsugi.md` and @io family-root discipline (io.mirror 80-92):
#
#   - PERMANENT @io: sha1 (git interop; SHAttered 2017 collisions
#     do not remove interop need); ed25519 primitives (constant-
#     time field arithmetic is crate-internal); age_encrypt /
#     age_decrypt (age is vendor crypto by construction);
#     aead_seal / aead_open (AEAD primitives depend on constant-
#     time platform intrinsics).
#   - CROSS-WALL-KINTSUGI CANDIDATE: sha256 (byte-level pure;
#     structurally-verified Rust impl imaginable per
#     [[architecture-cross-wall-kintsugi-candidate]]; fold deferred).
#
# Species shards under @io/crypto MAY refine the partition per
# specific primitive (forward-promised at species-altitude
# refinement).
#
# === Related shards / specs ===
#
# - boot/std/io/crypto.mirror (2026-06-01; the boot-floor grammar
#   this species lifts; retained as transitional placeholder
#   during consumer migration per the @cli + @mirror/data/json
#   precedent).
# - shards/io.mirror 161-162 (family-root vendor-surface naming).
# - shards/io/git.mirror (consumer; git object hashing).
# - shards/io/secrets.mirror (consumer; landed alongside this
#   lift-tick as Landing 4 of the @secrets shape-proposal
#   sequence).
# - shards/io/secrets/sops.mirror (consumer; landed alongside as
#   Landing 5; consumes age vendor backend).
# - docs/insights/2026-05-26-glass-wall-and-cross-wall-kintsugi.md
#   (the partition this species inherits).
# - docs/scouts/2026-07-15-mara-secrets-shape-proposal.md §5.5
#   step 6 (the landing sequence this shard discharges).
# - docs/audits/2026-07-15-seam-secrets-shape-proposal-phase-d-
#   cascade.md §D9 (the REED-INLINE cascade that named this
#   lift-tick as substrate-honest prerequisite).
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] (`prism @io/crypto`),
# [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]] (transparency inheritance
#   through @io),
# [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (grammar-altitude @io/crypto
#   → mirror-altitude @io/crypto species; the same lift that gave
#   @cli → @mirror/lens/cli and @data/json → @mirror/data/json),
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (~61st instance;
#   boot-floor grammar named the primitive since 2026-06-01; the
#   mirror-altitude species names what consumers already assumed
#   existed),
# [[feedback-substrate-pull]] (the family root pulls @io/crypto
#   from boot floor to mirror altitude; no invention, only lift),
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (key_material, ciphertext_bytes,
#   signature_bytes, aead_context are typed carriers; never bare
#   byte-refs at the boundary),
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (all action bodies `\`-obligation-
#   blocked; consumers pull the realization; Arc-1 evaluator FLOOR
#   pending).
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/io/crypto.mirror`
# declares `@io/crypto` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_
# namespace`.

# ============================================================
# §2 The carriers
# ============================================================

# === The key_material carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for cryptographic key material at the @io
# boundary. Per @io opacity discipline (io.mirror 66-72): the key
# BYTES are opaque by construction; the carrier holds a REF that
# resolves at the realisation boundary against out-of-substrate
# storage (.git/mirror-side per Alex 2026-07-14 SSH-signing intent).
#
# Two-field record:
#
#   algorithm    — typed ref naming the key algorithm (ed25519,
#                  age, ssh-rsa, ssh-ed25519, pgp, kms-recipient).
#                  The realisation dispatches on this field.
#   material_ref — typed ref into out-of-substrate key storage
#                  (.git/mirror-side per Fractal.Lens pointer
#                  discipline; NEVER projected into the git working
#                  tree; NEVER carried in-substrate as bytes).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (algorithm, material_ref).
type key_material = {
  algorithm:    ref,
  material_ref: ref,
}

# === The ciphertext_bytes carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for AEAD-produced ciphertext + associated data
# at the @io boundary. Opaque foreign blob per @io family-root
# discipline (io.mirror 37-40 Glass Wall: "foreign blobs ... must
# be under @io").
#
# Three-field record:
#
#   nonce         — the AEAD nonce (typed ref; per-scheme byte-
#                   length: 12 bytes for ChaCha20-Poly1305; 12 or
#                   16 for AES-GCM per scheme spec).
#   ciphertext    — the encrypted bytes + authentication tag
#                   (typed ref; AEAD-scheme-dependent tag layout).
#   associated_data — the authenticated-but-not-encrypted context
#                   (typed ref; empty ref admissible).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (nonce, ciphertext,
# associated_data).
type ciphertext_bytes = {
  nonce:           ref,
  ciphertext:      ref,
  associated_data: ref,
}

# === The signature_bytes carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for a cryptographic signature at the @io
# boundary. Opaque per @io opacity discipline.
#
# Three-field record:
#
#   algorithm  — typed ref naming the signature scheme (ed25519,
#                ecdsa-p256, rsa-pss, ssh-rsa). Per Alex
#                2026-07-14 SSH-signing design intent + Pack
#                commit convention: ed25519 is the substrate's
#                default; ssh-ed25519 is the substrate's SSH
#                signing surface.
#   signature  — the signature bytes (typed ref; scheme-dependent
#                length: 64 bytes for ed25519; variable for RSA).
#   public_key — the public-key material used to verify (typed
#                ref; ssh-key vendor surface per io.mirror 161-
#                162; carried alongside the signature for
#                Fractal.Lens pointer preservation — verification
#                does not require a separate key lookup).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (algorithm, signature,
# public_key).
type signature_bytes = {
  algorithm:  ref,
  signature:  ref,
  public_key: ref,
}

# === The aead_context carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for an AEAD-cipher context (algorithm + key +
# associated_data policy) at the @io boundary. Consumed by
# aead_seal / aead_open to name the cipher configuration a
# projection uses.
#
# Three-field record:
#
#   algorithm      — typed ref naming the AEAD scheme
#                    (chacha20-poly1305, aes-256-gcm, xchacha20-
#                    poly1305).
#   key            — key_material ref (the encryption key; MUST
#                    have algorithm matching an AEAD-compatible
#                    keygen scheme per the vendor library).
#   ad_policy      — typed ref naming the associated-data policy
#                    (empty, project_ref, per-realisation).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (algorithm, key, ad_policy).
type aead_context = {
  algorithm: ref,
  key:       key_material,
  ad_policy: ref,
}

# ============================================================
# §3 The actions
# ============================================================

# === sha1 action ===
#
# 20-byte SHA-1 digest. Lifted verbatim from boot/std/io/crypto.
# mirror. Retained per glass-wall recognition: SHA-1 is permanent
# @io (git interop; SHAttered 2017 collisions do not remove
# interop need). Total; every byte input has a canonical SHA-1.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (sha1 crate).
sha1(bytes: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === sha256 action ===
#
# 32-byte SHA-256 digest. Lifted verbatim from boot floor. The
# substrate's structural content-addressing function (per
# @fragmentation, @io/oci digest, Nix derivation hash; recognition
# #98 candidate territory).
#
# Cross-wall-kintsugi candidate (per the byte-level-pure partition
# in glass-wall insight); fold deferred; species shards may pull
# a structurally-verified impl when the substrate's analyzability
# matures.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (sha2 crate).
sha256(bytes: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === ed25519_sign action ===
#
# Ed25519 signature over msg under secret key. Output is 64-byte
# (R || s) per RFC 8032. Lifted verbatim from boot floor. Total
# at the signature layer; the signature is deterministic given
# (key, msg).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (ed25519-dalek).
ed25519_sign(key: key_material, msg: ref) -> signature_bytes { \ }

# === ed25519_verify action ===
#
# Verify sig against (pub_key, msg). Returns imperfect: success()
# iff signature is valid; failure with diagnostic iff malformed
# inputs (wrong length pub_key/sig, non-canonical encoding) or
# invalid signature. Lifted verbatim from boot floor.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (ed25519-dalek).
ed25519_verify(sig: signature_bytes, msg: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# === aead_seal action ===
#
# AEAD-authenticated encryption. Given an aead_context (algorithm
# + key + ad_policy) and plaintext bytes, produces ciphertext_bytes
# carrying (nonce, ciphertext+tag, associated_data). Nonce is
# generated per-invocation at the realisation boundary via
# @io/random.
#
# requires key_material_admissible(ctx.key): the AEAD context's
# key MUST be well-formed for the named algorithm.
#
# Returns imperfect<ciphertext_bytes, ref, ref>:
# - success(ciphertext_bytes) — encryption complete; ciphertext
#   is authenticated + decryptable by the corresponding open.
# - partial(ciphertext_bytes, transparency) — encryption complete
#   with residual (e.g., nonce reuse warning at realisation).
# - failure(error, transparency) — encryption failed (key mismatch,
#   algorithm unsupported, entropy source unavailable).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (aes-gcm /
# chacha20poly1305 crates; permanent-@io per crate-internal
# constant-time discipline).
aead_seal(ctx: aead_context, plaintext: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# === aead_open action ===
#
# AEAD-authenticated decryption. Inverse of aead_seal. Verifies
# the authentication tag against the ciphertext + associated_data;
# returns the recovered plaintext on success.
#
# requires key_material_admissible(ctx.key): the AEAD context's
# key MUST be well-formed for the named algorithm.
#
# Returns imperfect<ref, ref, ref>:
# - success(plaintext) — decryption complete; authentication tag
#   verified.
# - failure(error, transparency) — tag verification failed
#   (ciphertext tampering, wrong key, wrong associated_data,
#   wrong nonce).
#
# The Splinter/Narcissus discipline at AEAD altitude: aead_open
# MUST refuse to return plaintext when tag verification fails.
# A Narcissus-pole implementation that returns unauthenticated
# plaintext violates the AEAD contract.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
aead_open(ctx: aead_context, ct: ciphertext_bytes) -> imperfect { \ }

# === age_encrypt action ===
#
# The age vendor surface at @io/crypto altitude (per io.mirror
# 161-162 verbatim: "age" named as vendor surface). Encrypts
# plaintext bytes to one or more age recipients (age-encryption.org
# format; Valsorda 2019+). Composed by @io/secrets/sops's sops_
# encrypt when age is the key-group backend.
#
# requires recipients_admissible(recipients): the recipient list
# MUST be well-formed age recipients (X25519 public keys or
# ssh-ed25519 keys; refuses malformed recipients).
#
# Returns imperfect<ciphertext_bytes, ref, ref>:
# - success(ciphertext_bytes) — encryption complete; ciphertext
#   is decryptable by any recipient's private key.
# - failure(error, transparency) — encryption failed (recipient
#   parse error, algorithm unsupported).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (age crate).
# Permanent-@io per glass-wall partition (age IS vendor crypto).
age_encrypt(recipients: ref, plaintext: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# === age_decrypt action ===
#
# Inverse of age_encrypt. Decrypts an age-format ciphertext under
# an identity (age secret key or ssh-ed25519 key). Composed by
# @io/secrets/sops's sops_decrypt when age is the key-group
# backend.
#
# requires key_material_admissible(identity): the decryption
# identity MUST be a well-formed age identity.
#
# Returns imperfect<ref, ref, ref>:
# - success(plaintext) — decryption complete; recipient identity
#   matched.
# - failure(error, transparency) — decryption failed (identity
#   not in recipient list, ciphertext parse error, format
#   mismatch).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (age crate).
age_decrypt(identity: key_material, ct: ciphertext_bytes) -> imperfect { \ }

# === ssh_key_material action ===
#
# Load ssh-key vendor material (openssh-format public/private
# keys) as key_material carrier. Per io.mirror 161-162 verbatim
# ("ssh-key" named as vendor surface) + Alex 2026-07-14 SSH-
# signing design intent (peer keys are ssh-key vendor material
# stored .git/mirror-side).
#
# The material_ref carried on the returned key_material resolves
# through out-of-substrate storage per @io opacity discipline;
# the substrate NEVER carries the raw key bytes in-tree.
#
# requires ssh_key_ref_admissible(ref): the ref MUST resolve to a
# .git/mirror-side ssh key path.
#
# Returns imperfect<key_material, ref, ref>.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (ssh-key crate).
ssh_key_material(ssh_key_ref: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The bilaterals (Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude)
# ============================================================

# === key_material_admissible predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that a key_material carrier is well-formed:
#
#   1. algorithm resolves to a supported scheme (ed25519, age,
#      ssh-rsa, ssh-ed25519, pgp, kms-recipient).
#   2. material_ref resolves through out-of-substrate storage
#      (per @io opacity discipline; refuses in-tree key refs).
#   3. algorithm ↔ material shape agrees (ed25519 keys are 32
#      bytes; age recipients are X25519 or ssh-ed25519).
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude per Mara-B §4.5.5: reads only
# byte-visible empirical state (algorithm string; ref-resolution
# byte-length; scheme lookup); no program semantics.
#
# Splinter-pole: key material is well-formed; loadable by the
# named vendor crypto backend.
# Narcissus-pole: algorithm mismatch, in-tree key ref, malformed
# key bytes; loading would fail or (worse) silently succeed with
# wrong-key semantics.
key_material_admissible(km: key_material) -> verdict { \ }

# === recipients_admissible predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that an age-encryption recipient list is
# well-formed:
#
#   1. Every recipient parses as either an X25519 public key
#      (age1... format) or an ssh-ed25519 public key.
#   2. The list is non-empty (empty recipient list would produce
#      undecryptable ciphertext; substrate-decl refuses).
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude: reads only byte-visible
# recipient strings; no program semantics.
#
# Splinter-pole: every recipient is a valid age recipient;
# encryption produces decryptable ciphertext.
# Narcissus-pole: malformed recipients; empty list; encryption
# would silently produce ciphertext no one can open.
recipients_admissible(recipients: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === signature_valid predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that a signature_bytes carrier verifies
# against a message:
#
#   1. algorithm ↔ signature length agrees (ed25519 = 64 bytes;
#      scheme-dependent for other algorithms).
#   2. public_key ↔ algorithm agrees.
#   3. verify(sig, msg) discharges Pass at the realisation
#      boundary.
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude: reads only byte-visible
# signature + message state; verification is a bounded
# cryptographic operation.
#
# Splinter-pole: signature verifies against msg under pub_key.
# Narcissus-pole: verification fails or is bypassed.
signature_valid(sig: signature_bytes, msg: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === crypto_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at @io/crypto altitude for
# aead-projection contexts. Composes:
#
#   1. key_material_admissible(ctx.key)
#   2. algorithm-appropriate parameter shape (algorithm-specific
#      nonce length, tag length, key length agreement)
#
# Sibling to @io/oci.oci_well_formed, @io/git.git_well_formed,
# @io/algebra.io_algebra_well_formed — the composed-bilateral
# pattern at @io species altitude (per Seam tick 68 C4/C9
# closure).
#
# Splinter-pole: context is well-formed; aead_seal / aead_open
# discharge cleanly.
# Narcissus-pole: any sub-check fails; alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics (#57) distinguishes which claim broke.
crypto_well_formed(ctx: aead_context) -> verdict
requires key_material_admissible(ctx.key)
{ \ }

out @io/crypto
out key_material
out ciphertext_bytes
out signature_bytes
out aead_context
out sha1
out sha256
out ed25519_sign
out ed25519_verify
out aead_seal
out aead_open
out age_encrypt
out age_decrypt
out ssh_key_material
out key_material_admissible
out recipients_admissible
out signature_valid
out crypto_well_formed
